            },
            "displayName": "Paco Avila",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Madrid"
          },
          "body": "A query like this will fail:\n\n//element(*, nt:base)[jcr:contains(., 'test \\ done')]\n\nSpecification JSR-170 at point 6.6.5.2 says that literal instances like single quote ( ' ), double quote ( \" ) and hyphen ( - ) must be escaped with a backslash ( \\ ), and backslash itself should be escaped as a double backslash ( \\\\ ). Also, I have noted that some chars like [ and ] need to be escaped also.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=monkiki",
            "name": "monkiki",
            "key": "monkiki",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Paco Avila",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Madrid"
          },
          "created": "2010-03-01T19:36:18.203+0000",
          "updated": "2010-03-01T19:38:28.730+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12383602/comment/12839871",
          "id": "12839871",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=alexander.klimetschek",
            "name": "alexander.klimetschek",
            "key": "alexander.klimetschek",
